The compound described by the SMILES `Br.COc1ccc2c3c1O[C@H]1C[C@@H](O)C=C[C@@]31CCN(C)C2` is galanthamine hydrobromide (galantamine HBr), a well-known acetylcholinesterase inhibitor.

Galantamine's IC50 against acetylcholinesterase (AChE) has been widely reported. In ChEMBL, values for galantamine against human AChE (CHEMBL4078) are commonly reported in the range of approximately 500–2000 nM, with a frequently cited value around 1800 nM (though values vary by assay conditions). A commonly referenced IC50 value from ChEMBL is approximately 1700–1800 nM.

